# Machine-local settings. Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and edit per machine.
#
# Rule: this file says WHERE and ON WHAT MACHINE the experiment runs. The
# scientific recipe (model, data, learning rates, steps, batch sizes, seeds)
# lives only in configs/pilot/*.yaml, which is fingerprinted into run IDs.
# Execution knobs (micro-batch sizes, GPU count, checkpoint cadence) live in
# configs/runtime/*.yaml. Variables already set in the shell override this file.
# Relative paths are resolved against the repository folder.

# --- What to run ------------------------------------------------------------
# Experiment config used when a script gets no --config.
UNLEARNING_CONFIG=configs/pilot/qwen2.5-0.5b_laptop.yaml
# Runtime profile used when a script gets no --runtime.
#   laptop_8gb.yaml       this laptop (1 GPU, python launch)
#   cloud_1gpu_80gb.yaml  one rented A100/H100
#   cloud_ddp_4gpu.yaml   rented 4-GPU node (accelerate launch, DDP)
UNLEARNING_RUNTIME=configs/runtime/laptop_8gb.yaml

# --- Where everything is stored --------------------------------------------
# Root for data/, checkpoints/, runs/, results/ and hf_cache/. On a rented
# machine point this at the large volume (e.g. /workspace/unlearning-storage).
UNLEARNING_STORAGE_ROOT=.
# Hugging Face download cache (models + datasets). Default: <storage root>/hf_cache
# HF_HOME=D:/hf_cache
# Public models need no token, but anonymous downloads are rate-limited (HTTP 429).
# A free Hugging Face read token avoids that: https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens
HF_TOKEN=
HF_HUB_DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1
# Windows without Developer Mode cannot symlink; the cache then stores copies (fine).
HF_HUB_DISABLE_SYMLINKS_WARNING=1

# --- Hardware guard rails -----------------------------------------------------
# Refuse to train on a GPU with less memory than this (GB). 0 disables the check.
# The RTX 4070 Laptop reports ~8.0 GB. Use ~20 for 1.5B and ~40 for 3B runs.
UNLEARNING_MIN_GPU_MEMORY_GB=7.5
# Refuse to start, and stop before a checkpoint save, below this free disk (GB).
UNLEARNING_MIN_FREE_DISK_GB=15
# Pause between optimizer steps while the GPU is this hot (C), resume when it
# has cooled to the second value. Pausing never changes results. 0 disables.
UNLEARNING_GPU_PAUSE_TEMP_C=87
UNLEARNING_GPU_RESUME_TEMP_C=78

# --- GPU / runtime environment ------------------------------------------------
# Which GPUs this process sees. Laptop: 0. Multi-GPU node: 0,1,2,3
CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0
# Linux only (unsupported on Windows): reduces fragmentation-related out-of-memory errors.
# PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True
TOKENIZERS_PARALLELISM=false
